  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'The graph shows changes in pH for the titrations of equal volumes of solutions of two monoprotic acids, Acid 1 and Acid 2, with KOH(aq). Explain the differences between Acid 1 and Acid 2 in terms of their relative strengths and concentrations. (3 marks)', 'Strength: Acid 1 has a very low starting pH (about 1), stays low and then shows a long, steep rise at equivalence from about pH 3 to 11 - typical of a strong acid that is fully ionised. Acid 2 starts at a higher pH (about 2-4) even though it is more concentrated, shows a gently rising buffer region around pH 4-5 (half-equivalence pH ≈ pKa ≈ 4.5) and a shorter jump starting near pH 6, with an equivalence point above 7 - typical of a weak acid that is only partly ionised.
Concentration: the equivalence volume is about 25 mL of KOH for Acid 1 but about 37 mL for Acid 2. Since equal volumes of the two monoprotic acids were titrated, Acid 2 contains more moles of acid - it is about 37/25 ≈ 1.5 times more concentrated than Acid 1. So Acid 1 is stronger but more dilute; Acid 2 is weaker but more concentrated.', null, '[{"point": "Strength: Acid 1 starts at pH ≈ 1 with a long steep jump (≈ pH 3 to 11) - a strong acid; Acid 2 starts higher (pH ≈ 2-4), has a buffer region (pH ≈ 4-5) and a jump from ≈ 6 to 11 - a weak acid", "marks": 1.5}, {"point": "Concentration: equivalence needs ≈ 25 mL KOH for Acid 1 and ≈ 37 mL for Acid 2 → Acid 2 is more concentrated (≈ 1.5 times) since the volumes of acid are equal", "marks": 1.5}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge') and t.slug = 'engineering-general-subject-knowledge'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-technical-2'), 'standard', 3,
