  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'To check over-speeding vehicles, police use a radar speed gun. Explain the physics behind the working of a radar speed gun. (3 marks)', 'A radar speed gun works on the Doppler effect. It transmits a beam of radio (microwave) waves of a known frequency f towards the vehicle. The waves reflect off the vehicle and return to the gun. If the vehicle is moving, the reflected waves come back with a different frequency: higher if it is approaching, lower if it is moving away. The frequency shift is proportional to the vehicle''s speed: Δf ≈ 2vf/c (the factor 2 because the moving car both receives and re-emits the wave). The gun''s electronics compare the transmitted and received frequencies, compute v = cΔf/(2f) and display the speed instantly.', null, '[{"point": "The gun emits radio/ microwaves of known frequency towards the vehicle, which reflect back to the gun", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Doppler effect: the reflected waves from a moving vehicle have a shifted frequency (higher if approaching, lower if moving away)", "marks": 1}, {"point": "The shift Δf ≈ 2vf/c is measured electronically and converted into the vehicle''s speed v = cΔf/(2f)", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge') and t.slug = 'engineering-general-subject-knowledge'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-technical-2'), 'standard', 3,
